--- a/docs/content/archive.md
+++ b/docs/content/archive.md
@@ -120,6 +120,30 @@ $ rclone lsl --max-depth 1 :archive:s3:rclone/dir/100files.zip
 
 For `zip` and `squashfs` files this is 1s.
 
+## Symlinks
+
+Symbolic links stored in an archive are only exposed when
+`--links` (`-l`) is in use, following the convention of the
+[local](/local/) backend. Without it they are skipped and a notice is
+logged naming the flag.
+
+With `--links` a symlink is listed under its name plus the
+`.rclonelink` suffix, its size is the length of the link target, and
+reading it returns the target. This means a copy recreates the symlink
+on a destination which supports them:
+
+```
+$ rclone lsl --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip
+        5 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/file.txt
+        8 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/link.txt.rclonelink
+$ rclone copy --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip /tmp/out
+$ ls -l /tmp/out/src/link.txt
+lrwxr-xr-x 1 user user 8 Sep 28 14:16 /tmp/out/src/link.txt -> file.txt
+```
+
+A regular file in the archive whose name happens to end in
+`.rclonelink` is still exposed as a regular file.
+
 ## Hashes
 
 Which hash is supported depends on the archive type. Zip files use
